158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>86</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>EE1 Registered User (Browser) Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If EE1 Registered User (Browser) is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P1 Web Frontend Interface executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then EE1 Registered User (Browser) can tamper with P1 Web Frontend Interface. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Password reset request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T13.1f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>1</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Scripting</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>The web server 'P1 Web Frontend Interface' could be a subject to a cross-site scripting attack because it does not sanitize untrusted input.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Password reset request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T13.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>2</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P1 Web Frontend Interface may be able to impersonate the context of EE1 Registered User (Browser) in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Password reset request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T29fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a40d0c3e0e-7707-4e17-8c39-1dd5103dfa207bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0d0c3e0e-7707-4e17-8c39-1dd5103dfa20</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>3</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4:0d0c3e0e-7707-4e17-8c39-1dd5103dfa20:7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>P1 Web Frontend Interface Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If P1 Web Frontend Interface is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P2 Account Management Service executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then P1 Web Frontend Interface can tamper with P2 Account Management Service. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>forwarded password reset request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E59fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a40d0c3e0e-7707-4e17-8c39-1dd5103dfa207bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>0d0c3e0e-7707-4e17-8c39-1dd5103dfa20</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>4</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4:0d0c3e0e-7707-4e17-8c39-1dd5103dfa20:7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P2 Account Management Service may be able to impersonate the context of P1 Web Frontend Interface in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>forwarded password reset request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S7.17bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b22ea4198-0474-4f44-8309-3df5cc101133b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>22ea4198-0474-4f44-8309-3df5cc101133</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>5</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b:22ea4198-0474-4f44-8309-3df5cc101133:b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of Destination Data Store DS1 Backend User Database</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>DS1 Backend User Database may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of DS1 Backend User Database. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>user account verification query</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S7.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D27bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b22ea4198-0474-4f44-8309-3df5cc101133b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>22ea4198-0474-4f44-8309-3df5cc101133</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>6</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b:22ea4198-0474-4f44-8309-3df5cc101133:b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for P2 Account Management Service or DS1 Backend User Database</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Does P2 Account Management Service or DS1 Backend User Database take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>user account verification query</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T27bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b7697bb7b-2c0c-48eb-807c-0788d257e337bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>7697bb7b-2c0c-48eb-807c-0788d257e337</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>7</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b:7697bb7b-2c0c-48eb-807c-0788d257e337:bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>P2 Account Management Service Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If P2 Account Management Service is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P3 Password Reset Token Module executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then P2 Account Management Service can tamper with P3 Password Reset Token Module. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>token generation request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E57bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b7697bb7b-2c0c-48eb-807c-0788d257e337bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>7697bb7b-2c0c-48eb-807c-0788d257e337</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>8</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b:7697bb7b-2c0c-48eb-807c-0788d257e337:bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P3 Password Reset Token Module may be able to impersonate the context of P2 Account Management Service in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>token generation request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S3dac612cd-2bb2-44c7-9b13-1bd23b9cdfdf5317d084-e63b-4b34-b8e5-72a7e11cb6ddf3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5317d084-e63b-4b34-b8e5-72a7e11cb6dd</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>9</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>dac612cd-2bb2-44c7-9b13-1bd23b9cdfdf:5317d084-e63b-4b34-b8e5-72a7e11cb6dd:f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the External communication channel External Entity</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>External communication channel may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to EE1 Registered User (Browser). Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>password reset token</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>dac612cd-2bb2-44c7-9b13-1bd23b9cdfdf</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5dac612cd-2bb2-44c7-9b13-1bd23b9cdfdf5317d084-e63b-4b34-b8e5-72a7e11cb6ddf3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5317d084-e63b-4b34-b8e5-72a7e11cb6dd</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>10</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>dac612cd-2bb2-44c7-9b13-1bd23b9cdfdf:5317d084-e63b-4b34-b8e5-72a7e11cb6dd:f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>EE1 Registered User (Browser) may be able to impersonate the context of External communication channel in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>password reset token</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>dac612cd-2bb2-44c7-9b13-1bd23b9cdfdf</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T2f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acefcb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b79fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>cb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b7</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>11</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:cb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b7:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>EE1 Registered User (Browser) Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If EE1 Registered User (Browser) is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P1 Web Frontend Interface executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then EE1 Registered User (Browser) can tamper with P1 Web Frontend Interface. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>reset token and new password</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T13.1f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acefcb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b79fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>cb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b7</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>12</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:cb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b7:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Scripting</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>The web server 'P1 Web Frontend Interface' could be a subject to a cross-site scripting attack because it does not sanitize untrusted input.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>reset token and new password</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T13.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acefcb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b79fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>cb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b7</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>13</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:cb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b7:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P1 Web Frontend Interface may be able to impersonate the context of EE1 Registered User (Browser) in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>reset token and new password</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T29fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a484ef609c-af23-42f7-bf3f-e83672d931bf7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>84ef609c-af23-42f7-bf3f-e83672d931bf</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>14</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4:84ef609c-af23-42f7-bf3f-e83672d931bf:7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>P1 Web Frontend Interface Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If P1 Web Frontend Interface is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P2 Account Management Service executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then P1 Web Frontend Interface can tamper with P2 Account Management Service. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>forwarded reset token and new password</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E59fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a484ef609c-af23-42f7-bf3f-e83672d931bf7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>84ef609c-af23-42f7-bf3f-e83672d931bf</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>15</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4:84ef609c-af23-42f7-bf3f-e83672d931bf:7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P2 Account Management Service may be able to impersonate the context of P1 Web Frontend Interface in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>forwarded reset token and new password</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E57bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412baea674e6-2663-495e-a5a8-4aaf23134b77bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>aea674e6-2663-495e-a5a8-4aaf23134b77</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>239</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b:aea674e6-2663-495e-a5a8-4aaf23134b77:bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P3 Password Reset Token Module may be able to impersonate the context of P2 Account Management Service in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Token Validation Request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T27bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412baea674e6-2663-495e-a5a8-4aaf23134b77bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>aea674e6-2663-495e-a5a8-4aaf23134b77</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>238</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b:aea674e6-2663-495e-a5a8-4aaf23134b77:bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>P2 Account Management Service Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If P2 Account Management Service is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P3 Password Reset Token Module executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then P2 Account Management Service can tamper with P3 Password Reset Token Module. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Token Validation Request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>7bc3ad0a-861d-4e50-ae0e-4ba2d83e412b</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>bcb495da-b9be-41f8-9b35-b1e80df8a191</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T2f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef1c3b542c-dd78-4ff9-b706-d4eb4ef5ed299fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>1c3b542c-dd78-4ff9-b706-d4eb4ef5ed29</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>18</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:1c3b542c-dd78-