</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T13.1f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef1c3b542c-dd78-4ff9-b706-d4eb4ef5ed299fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>1c3b542c-dd78-4ff9-b706-d4eb4ef5ed29</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>19</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:1c3b542c-dd78-4ff9-b706-d4eb4ef5ed29:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Scripting</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>The web server 'P1 Web Frontend Interface' could be a subject to a cross-site scripting attack because it does not sanitize untrusted input.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>authenticated api request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T13.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef1c3b542c-dd78-4ff9-b706-d4eb4ef5ed299fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>1c3b542c-dd78-4ff9-b706-d4eb4ef5ed29</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>20</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:1c3b542c-dd78-4ff9-b706-d4eb4ef5ed29:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P1 Web Frontend Interface may be able to impersonate the context of EE1 Registered User (Browser) in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>authenticated api request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T29fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4861c9bd1-b5f9-4018-a7ea-cf9e59888cc6579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>861c9bd1-b5f9-4018-a7ea-cf9e59888cc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>21</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4:861c9bd1-b5f9-4018-a7ea-cf9e59888cc6:579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>P1 Web Frontend Interface Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If P1 Web Frontend Interface is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P4 User Profile API Handler executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then P1 Web Frontend Interface can tamper with P4 User Profile API Handler. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>forwarded authenticated API request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E59fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4861c9bd1-b5f9-4018-a7ea-cf9e59888cc6579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>861c9bd1-b5f9-4018-a7ea-cf9e59888cc6</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>22</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4:861c9bd1-b5f9-4018-a7ea-cf9e59888cc6:579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P4 User Profile API Handler may be able to impersonate the context of P1 Web Frontend Interface in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>forwarded authenticated API request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S7.1579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b653d96e07-97ff-47b0-8fa5-39cc4cfa90e5b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>53d96e07-97ff-47b0-8fa5-39cc4cfa90e5</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>23</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6:53d96e07-97ff-47b0-8fa5-39cc4cfa90e5:b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of Destination Data Store DS1 Backend User Database</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>DS1 Backend User Database may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to data being written to the attacker's target instead of DS1 Backend User Database. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>profile data query or update</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S7.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D2579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b653d96e07-97ff-47b0-8fa5-39cc4cfa90e5b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>53d96e07-97ff-47b0-8fa5-39cc4cfa90e5</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>24</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6:53d96e07-97ff-47b0-8fa5-39cc4cfa90e5:b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Excessive Resource Consumption for P4 User Profile API Handler or DS1 Backend User Database</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Does P4 User Profile API Handler or DS1 Backend User Database take explicit steps to control resource consumption? Resource consumption attacks can be hard to deal with, and there are times that it makes sense to let the OS do the job. Be careful that your resource requests don't deadlock, and that they do timeout.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>profile data query or update</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S7b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a29d19120-216d-4b8e-93a9-2d1231db5dab579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>29d19120-216d-4b8e-93a9-2d1231db5dab</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>25</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a:29d19120-216d-4b8e-93a9-2d1231db5dab:579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of Source Data Store DS1 Backend User Database</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>DS1 Backend User Database may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to incorrect data delivered to P4 User Profile API Handler. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>profile data response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>I23b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a29d19120-216d-4b8e-93a9-2d1231db5dab579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>29d19120-216d-4b8e-93a9-2d1231db5dab</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>26</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a:29d19120-216d-4b8e-93a9-2d1231db5dab:579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Weak Access Control for a Resource</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Improper data protection of DS1 Backend User Database can allow an attacker to read information not intended for disclosure. Review authorization settings.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>profile data response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>b1b96723-1065-4f89-a60f-842f2f2dae0a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I23</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T2579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6f7a0d7a3-d825-40a0-b4cd-8df0f86780ac9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f7a0d7a3-d825-40a0-b4cd-8df0f86780ac</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>27</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6:f7a0d7a3-d825-40a0-b4cd-8df0f86780ac:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>P4 User Profile API Handler Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If P4 User Profile API Handler is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P1 Web Frontend Interface executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then P4 User Profile API Handler can tamper with P1 Web Frontend Interface. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>api response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T13.1579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6f7a0d7a3-d825-40a0-b4cd-8df0f86780ac9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f7a0d7a3-d825-40a0-b4cd-8df0f86780ac</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>28</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6:f7a0d7a3-d825-40a0-b4cd-8df0f86780ac:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Scripting</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>The web server 'P1 Web Frontend Interface' could be a subject to a cross-site scripting attack because it does not sanitize untrusted input.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>api response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T13.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6f7a0d7a3-d825-40a0-b4cd-8df0f86780ac9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>f7a0d7a3-d825-40a0-b4cd-8df0f86780ac</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>29</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6:f7a0d7a3-d825-40a0-b4cd-8df0f86780ac:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P1 Web Frontend Interface may be able to impersonate the context of P4 User Profile API Handler in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>api response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>579f4a4a-e996-450d-8cd8-cf3a082528b6</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T29fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4cc3a11ae-ffe9-42fe-baf1-0bb8e5563809f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>cc3a11ae-ffe9-42fe-baf1-0bb8e5563809</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>30</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4:cc3a11ae-ffe9-42fe-baf1-0bb8e5563809:f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>P1 Web Frontend Interface Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If P1 Web Frontend Interface is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what EE1 Registered User (Browser) executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then P1 Web Frontend Interface can tamper with EE1 Registered User (Browser). Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Api response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E59fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4cc3a11ae-ffe9-42fe-baf1-0bb8e5563809f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>cc3a11ae-ffe9-42fe-baf1-0bb8e5563809</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>31</b:Id><b:InteractionK