yValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R6f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>97</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:57efb7b8-3749-46b6-aa58-925d925ddfeb:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by P1 Web Frontend Interface</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P1 Web Frontend Interface claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Password reset request</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E55144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54af9b995b-df77-49b6-8444-60d74adef0a23f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>af9b995b-df77-49b6-8444-60d74adef0a2</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>96</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54:af9b995b-df77-49b6-8444-60d74adef0a2:3f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P5 AI Account Support Assistant may be able to impersonate the context of P6 LLM Integration Service in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Processed AI Response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>3f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T25144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54af9b995b-df77-49b6-8444-60d74adef0a23f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>af9b995b-df77-49b6-8444-60d74adef0a2</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>95</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54:af9b995b-df77-49b6-8444-60d74adef0a2:3f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>P6 LLM Integration Service Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If P6 LLM Integration Service is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P5 AI Account Support Assistant executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then P6 LLM Integration Service can tamper with P5 AI Account Support Assistant. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Processed AI Response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>3f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5b69aa210-141c-4ae3-9c06-650a63d6fd11432171af-a026-452e-ad75-f84a4157a0465144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>432171af-a026-452e-ad75-f84a4157a046</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>94</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>b69aa210-141c-4ae3-9c06-650a63d6fd11:432171af-a026-452e-ad75-f84a4157a046:5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P6 LLM Integration Service may be able to impersonate the context of EE2 External LLM Provider in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Generated LLM Response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>b69aa210-141c-4ae3-9c06-650a63d6fd11</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S3b69aa210-141c-4ae3-9c06-650a63d6fd11432171af-a026-452e-ad75-f84a4157a0465144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>432171af-a026-452e-ad75-f84a4157a046</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>93</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>b69aa210-141c-4ae3-9c06-650a63d6fd11:432171af-a026-452e-ad75-f84a4157a046:5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the EE2 External LLM Provider External Entity</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>EE2 External LLM Provider may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to P6 LLM Integration Service. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Generated LLM Response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>b69aa210-141c-4ae3-9c06-650a63d6fd11</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E7f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acefcb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b79fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>cb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b7</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>113</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef:cb50683a-236e-4724-af7c-bdc6607138b7:9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in P1 Web Frontend Interface</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into P1 Web Frontend Interface in order to change the flow of program execution within P1 Web Frontend Interface to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>reset token and new password</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E53f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70d14a421e-cbba-498b-96da-47f6822dc47e5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>d14a421e-cbba-498b-96da-47f6822dc47e</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>92</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>3f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70:d14a421e-cbba-498b-96da-47f6822dc47e:5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>P6 LLM Integration Service may be able to impersonate the context of P5 AI Account Support Assistant in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Sanitized Prompt + Approved Context</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>3f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T23f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70d14a421e-cbba-498b-96da-47f6822dc47e5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>d14a421e-cbba-498b-96da-47f6822dc47e</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>91</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>3f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70:d14a421e-cbba-498b-96da-47f6822dc47e:5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>P5 AI Account Support Assistant Process Memory Tampered</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>If P5 AI Account Support Assistant is given access to memory, such as shared memory or pointers, or is given the ability to control what P6 LLM Integration Service executes (for example, passing back a function pointer.), then P5 AI Account Support Assistant can tamper with P6 LLM Integration Service. Consider if the function could work with less access to memory, such as passing data rather than pointers. Copy in data provided, and then validate it.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Sanitized Prompt + Approved Context</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>3f23560f-421b-430c-be02-543edafbfb70</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>5144cf9f-b767-403f-a857-68def8e73f54</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E79fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4cdc34062-a7ac-4881-80cd-c274fe4effccf3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>b8cca8a7-a71e-4495-8b8b-37910620c923</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>cdc34062-a7ac-4881-80cd-c274fe4effcc</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>272</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4:cdc34062-a7ac-4881-80cd-c274fe4effcc:f3765703-9d86-4cd4-8e1f-653327b0acef</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in EE1 Registered User (Browser)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into EE1 Registered User (Browser) in order to change the flow of program execution within EE1 Registered User (Browser) to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>AI Response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>9fb9158b-4329-4917-b6c5-2c961596a2a4</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f3765703-9d